{
  "_readme": "Hand-corrected (year, player_id) -> pro_team_id pairs where that season's own kona_player_info.json resolves to 0 (\"FA\") even though the player had a real MLB team for the whole labeled season. Root cause (see context/research/schema-decisions.md's 'MLB franchise data (pro_team_id) is per-season' section for the original, incomplete finding): ESPN keeps a fantasy season's player data mutable through the following offseason, up until that league's next keeper deadline locks it in. A handful of star free agents didn't re-sign until deep into that following offseason (in a few cases, the 2021-22 lockout froze all signings until March), so the snapshot this project reads for the labeled season is actually a frozen post-season/pre-next-season state, not an in-season one -- it reflects the moment just before the *next* draft, not the season itself. Confirmed against real season-by-season rosters for each entry below; add a new entry (with the same reasoning verified) rather than assuming every 0 is this bug -- some 0s are genuine deep-bench/low-ownership gaps.",
